WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.857
These are the key contracts.

00:00:01.857 --> 00:00:06.002
Scalar means one value. IN means membership.

00:00:06.002 --> 00:00:11.662
EXISTS means existence. ANY and ALL compare one value with a set.

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:16.582
Correlation means the inner query depends on the current outer row.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:22.412
A derived table means the inner query produces rows for the outer query to use.

00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:26.927
If you understand the meaning, you can rebuild the syntax when needed.

00:00:26.927 --> 00:00:32.747
Connect this idea to a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists.

00:00:32.747 --> 00:00:38.457
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.457 --> 00:00:46.077
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:46.077 --> 00:00:51.487
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.487 --> 00:00:57.299
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
